# arms/adult/loco/man_l: the man's left arm: sleeve, bracer, hand; the fighter's hand rests on a sheathed hilt (when armed)
# The arm library (P2b production, FOLK-BODY): every view carries regions (U upper arm: the first two sleeve rows; F
# forearm: the rest of the sleeve; C cuff: the leather bracer; H hand), so a garment's sleeve recolours one drawing (doll_
# resolve.cpp regionsOf: rags bare arms, apron / smock rolled sleeves, a jerkin's linen shirt, a coat's or robe's trimmed
# cuff; P2c gloves and gauntlets). THE ARM KEYS (a sleeve or armour part on the armR / armL channels draws the same keys,
# or it vanishes on those frames): idle; walk D/U fwd back, R/L B F N; run D/U runF, R/L runB runF; lap; L lie; fling
# (the fall's recoil, D U R/L); guard (armR: the drawn weapon's ready guard, D U R L, its `grip` mark); the off hand while
# a weapon is out (armL): D/U oidle ofwd oback orunF, L oidle oB oF oN orunB orunF, R oback.
# The slice (P2b wave 1, FOLK-BODY); A3's pixels are the reference (docs/ref/style_a3). Format: rpg/art/doll/doll.h.
use person
body man
role arms std
layer armNear
anchor shoulderL
keys armL
side L

view D key back origin 1 -1
mark handL 0 5
|765
|765
|765
|hgf
